00:06:25,263 --> 00:06:31,263
Some missions need a hitman...others need a soldier.

2
00:12:50,526 --> 00:12:56,526
Sicario: Day of the Soldado is a action, crime,
thriller film directed by Stefano Sollima.

3
00:19:15,789 --> 00:19:21,789
Agent Matt Graver teams up with operative Alejandro Gillick to prevent Mexican drug
cartels from smuggling terrorists across the United States border.

4
00:25:41,052 --> 00:25:47,052
Alejandro Gillick, played by Benicio del Toro.

5
00:32:06,315 --> 00:32:12,315
Matt Graver, played by Josh Brolin.

6
00:38:31,578 --> 00:38:37,578
Isabel Reyes, played by Isabela Merced.

7
00:44:56,842 --> 00:45:02,842
Steve Forsing, played by Jeffrey Donovan.

8
00:51:22,105 --> 00:51:28,105
Cynthia Foards, played by Catherine Keener.

9
00:57:47,368 --> 00:57:53,368
Gallo, played by Manuel Garcia-Rulfo.

10
01:04:12,631 --> 01:04:18,631
Sicario: Day of the Soldado (also known as Sicario 2: Soldado or simply Soldado) is a 2018 American
action crime thriller film directed by Stefano Sollima and written by Taylor Sheridan.

11
01:10:37,894 --> 01:10:43,894
A sequel to 2015's Sicario, the film features Benicio del Toro, Josh Brolin, Jeffrey Donovan and Raoul Trujillo
reprising their roles, with Isabela Merced, Manuel Garcia-Rulfo and Catherine Keener joining the cast.

12
01:17:03,157 --> 01:17:09,157
The story relates to human trafficking at the U.S.–Mexico border and a covert effort by the
United States government to incite increased conflict among the cartels.

13
01:23:28,421 --> 01:23:34,421
Sicario: Day of the Soldado was released in the United States and Canada on June 29, 2018, by Sony Pictures Releasing under its Columbia Pictures
label, while it was distributed internationally by Lionsgate (excluding Latin America and Spain, where it was distributed by Sony).

14
01:29:53,684 --> 01:29:59,684
The film is dedicated to the memory of Jóhann Jóhannsson, the composer of
the first film, who died four months before it came out.

15
01:36:18,947 --> 01:36:24,947
It received generally favorable reviews from critics.

16
01:42:44,210 --> 01:42:50,210
A sequel, titled Sicario: Capos, is in development.

17
01:49:09,473 --> 01:49:15,473
The film explores themes of rescue, central intelligence agency
(cia), corruption, usa–mexico border, sequel.

18
01:55:34,736 --> 01:55:40,736
The tone is dark and intense.
